  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 A NEW session goes to the least-loaded healthy node; a returning one goes back
 to its match's node (session affinity). Affinity that outlives the node's
 health is worse than none: it sends every reconnect to a failing box.

Section: Is A Backend Still There

 Affinity is checked against the LIVE registry rather than against the
 session table alone. The session table records what was decided; only the
 group knows whether it is still true.

  mesh-backend-live : List ServiceLocation, Text, Integer -> Boolean
  mesh-backend-live (locs) (member) (i) =
    if i >= list-length locs then False
    else let l = list-at locs i
    in if l.sl-member-id == member then svc-is-healthy l
    else mesh-backend-live locs member (i + 1)

  mesh-backend-healthy : GroupState, EdgeRegion, Text -> Boolean
  mesh-backend-healthy (g) (r) (member) =
    mesh-backend-live (gs-find-service g (mesh-region-service r)) member 0

Section: Routing A Player

  MeshRoute =
    | RoutedSticky (Text)
    | RoutedFresh (Text)
    | RouteRefused (Text)

 A route says whether the session resumed or is new; without that, a working
 affinity table and one that re-picks every time look identical.

  mesh-route : GroupState, SessionTable, EdgeRegion, Text -> MeshRoute
  mesh-route (g) (tbl) (r) (player-key) =
    when stbl-find tbl player-key
      is Just (s) ->
        if mesh-backend-healthy g r (s.ss-backend) then RoutedSticky (s.ss-backend)
        else mesh-route-fresh g r
      is None -> mesh-route-fresh g r

  mesh-route-fresh : GroupState, EdgeRegion -> MeshRoute
  mesh-route-fresh (g) (r) =
    when gs-pick-load-balanced g (mesh-region-service r)
      is None -> RouteRefused ("region " & r.er-name & " has no healthy node")
      is Just (loc) -> RoutedFresh (loc.sl-member-id)

  mesh-route-member : MeshRoute -> Text
  mesh-route-member (rt) =
    when rt
      is RoutedSticky (m) -> m
      is RoutedFresh (m) -> m
      is RouteRefused (why) -> ""

 Routing does not remember: a caller that routes without remembering gets no
 affinity.

  mesh-remember : SessionTable, Text, MeshRoute, Integer -> SessionTable
  mesh-remember (tbl) (player-key) (rt) (now) =
    let m = mesh-route-member rt
    in if m == "" then tbl else stbl-set tbl player-key m now

Section: Reporting

  mesh-route-label : MeshRoute -> Text
  mesh-route-label (rt) =
    when rt
      is RoutedSticky (m) -> "sticky to " & m
      is RoutedFresh (m) -> "fresh to " & m
      is RouteRefused (why) -> "refused: " & why
